Thought: The ranking is unstable and many models are correlated, so a robust combination of the most stable models with inverse-error weighting may beat the current dba.  
Action: select_stable  
Action Input: {"k":5}

Thought: Try a robust trimmed mean on the stable pool1 to reduce influence of the few high‑error models while still leveraging most of the good ones.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2,"rationale":"robust trimmed mean on the stable 5‑model pool"}

Thought: The pool has many correlated models; pruning redundancy should give a cleaner set for weighted combinations.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: Create an inverse‑error weight vector on the pruned, low‑correlation pool (pool4) to see if weighted averaging beats the current leader dba.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: Test a simple weighted mean using the inverse‑error weights (w2) on the reduced, non‑redundant pool to see if it beats the current best robust baseline.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w2","rationale":"robust weighted mean on the reduced pool"}

Thought: Test shrinkage on inverse-error weighting for the reduced pool and for the stable pool, and try a median on the reduced pool to see if a more robust mean can beat dba.

Action: weights_inverse_error
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.2}

Thought: Evaluate the weighted mean with the new shrinkage handle on the reduced pool.

Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w4","pool":"pool4","rationale":"shrinked inverse-error on reduced pool"}

Thought: Evaluate the weighted mean with shrinkage on the stable 5‑model pool.

Action: weights_inverse_error
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.2}

Thought: Evaluate the weighted mean on the stable pool with shrinkage.

Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w5","pool":"pool1","rationale":"shrinked inverse-error on stable pool"}

Thought: Try a median combination on the reduced pool to see if a more robust statistic helps.

Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"median on reduced pool"}

Thought: The current best weighted mean (w2) is slightly above the leader; adding shrinkage (w4) may reduce variance and improve robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w4","rationale":"robust weighted mean with shrinkage on reduced pool"}

Thought: Test a robust median on the reduced, stable pool4 to see if it beats the current dba leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"robust median on reduced stable pool"}

Thought: test weighted inverse error with moderate shrinkage on the reduced pool to see if it beats the median.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5}  

Thought: evaluate the weighted combination using the new weights handle.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w5","rationale":"inverse error with moderate shrinkage"}  

Thought: create a very small pool of the top 3 models by error for a focused median.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":3,"metric":"rmse","windows":null}  

Thought: evaluate a robust median on the top‑3 pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool5","rationale":"median on top 3 models"}  

Thought: test weighted inverse error on the top‑3 pool with the same shrinkage.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool5","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5}  

Thought: evaluate the weighted combination on the top‑3 pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w7","rationale":"inverse error on top 3 models"}

Thought: Test the weighted mean using the inverse-error handle w6 (high shrinkage) to see if a near-uniform weighting improves on the median pool4 baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w6","rationale":"weighted mean with highly shrunk inverse-error weights"}

Thought: Try a trimmed mean on the robust pool4 to see if trimming extremes improves over the median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2,"rationale":"trim extremes on robust pool"}

Thought: The current best uses a robust median on a reduced pool. To reduce correlated error further, prune redundant models and try weighted inverse-error combinations on the pruned set.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: Try a weighted combination using the precomputed inverse-error weights w2 to see if a more data-driven weighting can beat the robust median on pool4.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w2","rationale":"test inverse-error weighting on full pool"}

Thought: Try a forward‑selection weighted combination on the full pool to see if a data‑driven weighting can beat the robust median on pool4.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with unstable model ranking; a robust median on the reduced, stable pool (pool4) aligns with the robust combination hint and gives the lowest validation score.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"robust median on reduced stable pool for trend‑dominated series"}

